+{"verdict":"FAIL","summary":"Dims 1-3 check out: the composed `depol ⊗ depol → BSM` map is a 64-Kraus TP channel, the default-path extraction math matches an independent prepare-and-measure enumeration, and the reported MDI finding is real in the small-`q` limit (`e_eff` fits `4q/3 - 8q^2/9`, so `4/3` is the correct first-order coefficient). Dims 4-6 are not clean enough to pass. The main problem is that the public `build_mdi_bell_protocol(qber)` still has a qber-independent executed/default path, so the new extractor is not safely integrable there as-is; `scope_reason` still says the blocker is merely “default path not implemented,” which is no longer the actual blocker after this patch. I could not run `pytest` in this sandbox because no writable temp directory is available, so the review is based on patch inspection plus direct Python checks.","issues":[{"severity":"major","category":"correctness","location":"qkdx/protocols/mdi.py:346-359","description":"`build_mdi_bell_protocol(qber)` still builds `net = mdi_bell_charlie_network()` with no per-arm depolarizing channel, and `mdi_alice_source` / `mdi_bob_source` do not encode `qber`. So `executed_state()` is identical for all `qber`, and `_mdi_bell_conditional_from_executed(build_mdi_bell_protocol(q))` returns the zero-noise `[0.5, 0, 0, 0.5]` state for every `q`. That means the public builder’s executed/default semantics are fundamentally incompatible with its `qber` parameter; the remaining gap is not just “missing default-path plumbing.”","suggestion":"Either expose a separate explicitly named physical builder that uses `mdi_full_physical_channel(qber)`, or document/guard `build_mdi_bell_protocol` so its executed path cannot be mistaken for a qber-aware default path. Do not wire `_mdi_bell_conditional_from_executed` into this builder until the convention is resolved."},{"severity":"major","category":"correctness","location":"qkdx/protocols/mdi.py:329-384","description":"The scope documentation is stale after Stage B.2. `scope_reason` and the builder docstring still say the protocol is partial because the default path is “not implemented” and deferred to Stage B.2, but this patch already adds `_mdi_bell_conditional_from_executed`. The actual remaining blocker is the unresolved override-vs-physical `qber` convention and the fact that the public builder still does not use the physical channel. Leaving the old reason in place misstates why `scope_tag` remains `partial`.","suggestion":"Update `scope_reason` and the builder docstring to say the default extractor exists in prototype form, but `covered` is blocked by unresolved `qber` semantics / physical-channel integration. Add a regression test that asserts the documented blocker explicitly."},{"severity":"minor","category":"error_handling","location":"qkdx/protocols/mdi.py:225-256","description":"`mdi_full_physical_channel()` is a new public helper but does not validate `qber`. For negative inputs it silently builds Kraus operators containing `NaN` values via `bb84_channel()`, instead of failing fast like the protocol builders do.","suggestion":"Add the same `0 <= qber <= 1` validation used by `build_mdi_protocol()` / `build_mdi_bell_protocol()`, and add tests for negative and >1 inputs."},{"severity":"minor","category":"test_coverage","location":"tests/test_protocols/test_mdi_bell.py:233-258","description":"The three `[FIND]` tests do capture the qualitative fact that the physical-path effective error is not equal to the input parameter, but they only exercise a private test-only helper and the `5e-3` absolute tolerance is loose for a claim that is now central to scope decisions. A materially different mapping could still pass.","suggestion":"Tighten the check against the observed quadratic (`e_eff = 4q/3 - 8q^2/9` for the current channel choice) or otherwise reduce the tolerance and add an assertion that the public builder remains intentionally non-physical until the convention decision is made."}],"round_recommendation":"First separate or explicitly guard the qber-aware physical path from `build_mdi_bell_protocol`, then update `scope_reason`/docs to reflect the real blocker, and finally tighten the `[FIND]` regression tests and add input validation for `mdi_full_physical_channel()`."}
